# Typing at the SA-1510 monitor prompt, which only the tape cases touched.
# SA-1510 letters: unshifted PC keys give capitals and Shift gives
# lowercase (see mz80a_insert.keys).
# SA-1510's commands are only J, L, F and B, so a line that isn't one
# just gets a fresh prompt.
150 type "qwertyuiop QWERTYUIOP 1234567890"
406 key Return
# A line with lowercase and shifted symbols, left unentered.
434 type "QABC abc 123 !\"#$%&'()=@[]"
